---
title: "dynamic_field::remove (Sui Move Concepts: Dynamic Field Removal)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_get_addr: object_addr = object.to_address()
    q_get_addr --> q_hash: hash = hash_type_and_key(object_addr, name)
    q_hash --> q_remove: Field { id, name, value } = remove_child_object(object_addr, hash)
    q_remove --> q_check_type: verify Field type matches Name and Value
    q_check_type --> q_delete_id: types match
    q_check_type --> q_abort_type: type mismatch
    q_delete_id --> q_return: id.delete()
    q_return --> [*]: return value

    q_abort_type --> [*]: abort - type mismatch or field not found

    note right of q_remove
        INV-001: Requires mutable reference to parent UID
        INV-002: Field must exist or transaction aborts
        INV-003: Returns the unwrapped value by move (ownership transferred to caller)
    end note

    note right of q_delete_id
        INV-004: Field wrapper UID is deleted after extraction
        INV-005: Returned value can be transferred, deleted, or used freely
    end note

    note right of q_return
        INV-006: Future access to removed field will abort
        INV-007: For dynamic_object_field, returned object regains independent ID accessibility
    end note
